Description: Add source_tarball conditions to chromium DEPS for tarball builds
 This patch adds 'condition': 'not source_tarball' to prevent git operations
 when building from Debian-provided chromium tarball sources.
 .
 Modified sections:
 - Five hooks (lastchange, gpu_lists_version, lastchange_skia, lastchange_dawn, lastchange_commit_position_cros)
 - EIGHT dependency entries:
   * webvr_info, crossbench, crossbench-web-tests, dom_distiller_js, crabbyavif (from Build 93)
   * clang-format/script, canvas_bench, content_analysis_sdk, crc32c (added Build 140 for chromium 142.0.7444.134)
 .
 Build 140 update: Added 4 missing dependencies discovered from Build 139 git fetch errors.
 These dependencies were NOT covered in original patch for chromium 142.0.7444.59
 and caused network isolation violations (git clone/fetch operations).
 .
 This eliminates all git fetch/clone operations during Phase 2a build,
 ensuring compliance with Debian's no-internet build policy.
 .
 Regenerated for Debian chromium 142.0.7444.162 with correct line numbers (Build 175k)
Author: Debian CEF Maintainers
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-15

